// expect: 10
// The three walks agree through a mask (LENS §2.3 (b)): `run`'s callback
// cell sits behind h's mask, and the quantifier reaches it exactly as the
// flatten does, so each caller instantiates its own copy — `a`'s `!F` never
// meets `b`'s F. A walk that stopped at the mask would leave one scratch
// cell shared by both callers, neither dropped nor quantified, and refuse
// `a` for an effect it never performs.
effect E { op() -> Int }
effect F { fop() -> Int }
handler h { op() => resume(7) }
handler hf { fop() => resume(3) }
fn run(f) = (f()) ~> h
fn a() with !F = run(() => op())
fn b() = (run(() => fop())) ~> hf
fn main() = a() + b()
